{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "skipLibCheck": true,

    /* Bundler mode. allowImportingTsExtensions lets every import carry an
       explicit .ts/.tsx suffix, which is what makes `node --test src/core/...`
       work without a build step. Vite resolves these fine. */
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,

    /* Keeping @types/vexflow out of the program.
       ------------------------------------------
       opensheetmusicdisplay@2.1.3 lists @types/vexflow@1.x among its runtime
       dependencies, so npm always installs it. Its last lines are:

           declare module "vexflow" { export = Vex; }

       That is an AMBIENT module declaration, and one of those outranks the
       real package's types, a `paths` mapping, everything. Every
       `import { Stave } from 'vexflow'` was checked against VexFlow 1's
       single `Vex` export and reported as having no such member, while
       --traceResolution cheerfully showed the correct 4.2.5 files being
       resolved. The resolver and the checker disagreed, and only the
       resolver was talking.

       Two doors had to be shut. `types` stops the automatic inclusion of
       everything under node_modules/@types. That alone is not enough: a
       `/// <reference types="vexflow" />` inside a dependency's own .d.ts
       pulls the shim in regardless. typeRoots is searched in order, so
       ./types/vexflow — which declares nothing — answers that reference
       first and the real package types stand.

       Both settings govern GLOBAL inclusion only. react and react-dom stay
       fully typed, because importing them resolves @types/react normally.
       Delete ./types/vexflow and the six errors come straight back. */
    "types": ["node"],
    "typeRoots": ["./types", "./node_modules/@types"],
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",

    /* Linting */
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "exactOptionalPropertyTypes": false
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
